1
00:00:00,825 --> 00:00:02,204
Last time, we asked:

2
00:00:02,224 --> 00:00:04,034
Two ring magnets on a pencil!

3
00:00:04,294 --> 00:00:07,824
The top one floats in mid-air, with no glue and no string.

4
00:00:08,104 --> 00:00:09,324
What holds it up?

5
00:00:09,377 --> 00:00:10,527
One, a pull.

6
00:00:11,767 --> 00:00:12,817
Two, a push.

7
00:00:14,288 --> 00:00:15,798
Hold on to your answer!

8
00:00:17,670 --> 00:00:21,130
Today, we find out where a magnet pulls the hardest, and how

9
00:00:21,150 --> 00:00:22,460
a magnet can push!

10
00:00:22,967 --> 00:00:25,447
A little spider is hiding in this video.

11
00:00:25,697 --> 00:00:26,937
Can you spot it?

12
00:00:27,058 --> 00:00:28,918
Spiders love quiet corners.

13
00:00:28,978 --> 00:00:30,258
Look in the corners!

14
00:00:30,309 --> 00:00:31,769
You against the Buddies!

15
00:00:32,039 --> 00:00:33,889
Lock in first with your fingers.

16
00:00:34,159 --> 00:00:35,989
One finger for every point.

17
00:00:36,570 --> 00:00:37,720
Today you'll learn:

18
00:00:37,922 --> 00:00:38,942
Two poles.

19
00:00:39,139 --> 00:00:40,689
Where the pull is strongest.

20
00:00:40,888 --> 00:00:42,238
Attract and repel.

21
00:00:42,740 --> 00:00:43,680
Are you ready?

22
00:00:44,120 --> 00:00:44,890
Three!

23
00:00:45,270 --> 00:00:45,930
Two!

24
00:00:46,300 --> 00:00:46,950
One!

25
00:00:47,370 --> 00:00:48,090
Go!

26
00:00:49,479 --> 00:00:50,369
Round one!

27
00:00:50,689 --> 00:00:52,269
What holds up the top ring?

28
00:00:52,559 --> 00:00:53,869
Show me your fingers!

29
00:00:57,340 --> 00:00:58,320
Locked in!

30
00:00:58,448 --> 00:00:59,318
One, a pull!

31
00:00:59,688 --> 00:01:02,098
Magnets attract, and attract means pull.

32
00:01:02,178 --> 00:01:03,878
We learnt that last time!

33
00:01:03,926 --> 00:01:04,806
Two.

34
00:01:04,976 --> 00:01:07,866
When I press the top ring down, I can feel it pushing

35
00:01:07,886 --> 00:01:09,336
back up on my finger.

36
00:01:09,384 --> 00:01:10,314
Two, a push!

37
00:01:10,444 --> 00:01:12,664
A pull would bring it down onto the other ring.

38
00:01:12,864 --> 00:01:14,624
Something must be pushing it up!

39
00:01:14,900 --> 00:01:16,470
Be the top ring magnet!

40
00:01:16,750 --> 00:01:17,740
Shrink down.

41
00:01:18,020 --> 00:01:18,950
Quietly.

42
00:01:21,235 --> 00:01:24,905
You are a ring magnet, sliding down a pencil like a pole

43
00:01:24,925 --> 00:01:26,005
at the playground.

44
00:01:26,755 --> 00:01:29,115
Below you is another ring magnet.

45
00:01:29,640 --> 00:01:31,470
Closer, and you slow down.

46
00:01:32,250 --> 00:01:34,960
Something you cannot see is pushing up on you.

47
00:01:35,740 --> 00:01:38,310
You stop in mid-air, and bob gently.

48
00:01:38,818 --> 00:01:40,258
Pip presses you down.

49
00:01:41,038 --> 00:01:43,368
The closer you get, the harder the push.

50
00:01:44,148 --> 00:01:46,258
He lets go, and up you spring!

51
00:01:46,771 --> 00:01:47,791
Look down.

52
00:01:48,561 --> 00:01:51,441
Between the rings is a gap with nothing in it.

53
00:01:52,211 --> 00:01:53,941
No glue, and no string.

54
00:01:54,801 --> 00:01:55,911
Just a push.

55
00:01:57,562 --> 00:01:59,472
The answer is two: a push!

56
00:01:59,722 --> 00:02:01,302
Did you show two fingers?

57
00:02:01,542 --> 00:02:02,942
Put one finger up!

58
00:02:02,962 --> 00:02:05,532
The bottom ring pushes up on the top ring.

59
00:02:05,692 --> 00:02:07,882
So the top ring floats on the push!

60
00:02:08,009 --> 00:02:10,739
Which part of a magnet pulls and pushes the most?

61
00:02:10,829 --> 00:02:13,999
I think it is the middle, because it is the biggest part!

62
00:02:14,648 --> 00:02:15,798
Look closer.

63
00:02:16,388 --> 00:02:19,918
Dip a bar magnet into the steel paper clips from our class

64
00:02:19,938 --> 00:02:21,271
stationery tray.

65
00:02:21,291 --> 00:02:22,391
Lift it up.

66
00:02:23,001 --> 00:02:25,451
The clips hang in bunches at the two ends.

67
00:02:26,021 --> 00:02:27,714
The middle has hardly any.

68
00:02:27,734 --> 00:02:30,474
These two ends are the magnet's poles.

69
00:02:31,734 --> 00:02:34,974
Every magnet has two poles: a North pole and a South pole.

70
00:02:34,994 --> 00:02:39,552
On this magnet, North is painted red, and South is painted blue!

71
00:02:39,572 --> 00:02:43,972
The bar magnet has the strongest pull or attraction at the two

72
00:02:43,992 --> 00:02:44,872
poles.

73
00:02:45,998 --> 00:02:48,218
Attraction is another word for the pull.

74
00:02:48,298 --> 00:02:51,174
It is strongest at the two poles, not in the middle!

75
00:02:51,194 --> 00:02:54,264
Every magnet has two poles, whatever its shape.

76
00:02:54,824 --> 00:02:58,364
A ring magnet's poles are on its two flat sides, one on

77
00:02:58,384 --> 00:03:00,434
top, and one underneath.

78
00:03:03,131 --> 00:03:04,431
Say it with me!

79
00:03:05,140 --> 00:03:06,860
A magnet has two poles.

80
00:03:07,330 --> 00:03:09,390
It has a North pole and a South pole.

81
00:03:09,920 --> 00:03:13,270
A magnet has two poles where attraction is the strongest.

82
00:03:15,897 --> 00:03:16,977
My turn!

83
00:03:17,197 --> 00:03:20,307
The top ring will not come down to touch the other ring.

84
00:03:20,557 --> 00:03:23,417
Magnets attract, so this ring must be broken!

85
00:03:23,546 --> 00:03:25,106
Something is not right.

86
00:03:25,376 --> 00:03:27,556
If you can spot it, cross your arms.

87
00:03:27,836 --> 00:03:28,796
Hold on!

88
00:03:34,209 --> 00:03:35,339
Arms crossed?

89
00:03:35,609 --> 00:03:36,819
One finger up!

90
00:03:36,871 --> 00:03:39,851
Watch! I turn the top ring over and let it go.

91
00:03:40,061 --> 00:03:40,711
Click!

92
00:03:40,871 --> 00:03:42,231
It snaps right down.

93
00:03:42,341 --> 00:03:43,871
It is not broken at all!

94
00:03:43,997 --> 00:03:46,497
The floating ring was pushed, not broken.

95
00:03:46,625 --> 00:03:49,095
So the same two magnets can push and pull?

96
00:03:49,175 --> 00:03:50,555
How does that work?

97
00:03:51,206 --> 00:03:52,336
Look closer.

98
00:03:52,916 --> 00:03:56,627
Two bar magnets lie on round pencils, so they can roll.

99
00:03:56,647 --> 00:04:00,457
A red end and a blue end: they roll together and click,

100
00:04:00,477 --> 00:04:01,960
even before they touch.

101
00:04:01,980 --> 00:04:03,490
Now turn one round.

102
00:04:04,060 --> 00:04:06,940
Two red ends: one magnet rolls away.

103
00:04:07,510 --> 00:04:09,067
The gap never closes.

104
00:04:09,087 --> 00:04:13,047
When magnets push each other away, we say they repel.

105
00:04:14,347 --> 00:04:15,577
Repel means push!

106
00:04:15,647 --> 00:04:18,735
Magnets can push each other away, without even touching!

107
00:04:18,755 --> 00:04:21,585
And it depends on which poles are facing each other!

108
00:04:24,290 --> 00:04:25,440
Say it with me!

109
00:04:26,152 --> 00:04:29,132
Magnets can attract (pull) or repel (push) one another.

110
00:04:29,842 --> 00:04:32,652
This depends on which poles are facing each other.

111
00:04:35,127 --> 00:04:36,587
Show me your score hand!

112
00:04:36,867 --> 00:04:37,897
Two fingers?

113
00:04:38,177 --> 00:04:39,547
You beat the Buddies.

114
00:04:39,827 --> 00:04:40,827
High five!

115
00:04:41,405 --> 00:04:42,865
Did you spot the spider?

116
00:04:43,145 --> 00:04:45,855
It was hanging on its silk thread, under the bench!

117
00:04:45,995 --> 00:04:47,305
Here is a fun fact!

118
00:04:47,375 --> 00:04:49,985
Many baby spiders can fly with no wings.

119
00:04:50,045 --> 00:04:52,985
They let out long silk threads, and the wind lifts them up

120
00:04:53,005 --> 00:04:54,055
into the sky!

121
00:04:54,180 --> 00:04:55,460
Tell someone at home!

122
00:04:56,189 --> 00:04:58,389
Let's read today's key words together!

123
00:04:58,679 --> 00:04:59,439
Ready?

124
00:04:59,726 --> 00:05:00,476
Poles.

125
00:05:01,904 --> 00:05:02,884
Attraction.

126
00:05:04,337 --> 00:05:05,167
Repel.

127
00:05:06,524 --> 00:05:07,464
Well done!

128
00:05:08,261 --> 00:05:10,061
A red end and a blue end pull.

129
00:05:10,191 --> 00:05:11,511
Two red ends push.

130
00:05:11,541 --> 00:05:13,161
But what about two blue ends?

131
00:05:13,241 --> 00:05:14,261
Is there a rule?

132
00:05:14,281 --> 00:05:15,871
Find out in Part Two!

133
00:05:17,031 --> 00:05:18,132
Say it with us!

134
00:05:18,932 --> 00:05:19,682
Ready?

135
00:05:19,806 --> 00:05:20,466
One!

136
00:05:20,806 --> 00:05:21,506
two!

137
00:05:21,811 --> 00:05:22,986
Now you know!
